{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["macOS"],"tokens":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"color","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLColor","text":"MXLColor","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL8MXLColorV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}]}]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLLyric\/color","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"kind":"symbol","sections":[],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxllyric\/color"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"metadata":{"role":"symbol","externalID":"s:7IvorMXL8MXLLyricV5colorAA8MXLColorVSgvp","modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}],"roleHeading":"Instance Property","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"color","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLColor","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL8MXLColorV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"title":"color","symbolKind":"property"},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The color attribute group indicates the color of an element."}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLLyric"]]},"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLLyric":{"type":"topic","title":"MXLLyric","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLLyric"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxllyric","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLLyric","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLLyric"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The lyric type represents text underlays for lyrics. Two text elements that are not separated by an elision"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"element are part of the same syllable, but may have different text formatting. The MusicXML XSD is more strict"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"than the DTD in enforcing this by disallowing a second syllabic element unless preceded by an elision element."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"The lyric number indicates multiple lines, though a name can be used as well. Common name examples are verse"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and chorus."}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLLyric/color":{"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLLyric\/color","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxllyric\/color","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"color"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL8MXLColorV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MXLColor"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}],"title":"color","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The color attribute group indicates the color of an element."}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLColor":{"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlcolor","title":"MXLColor","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLColor"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLColor"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The color type indicates the color of an element. Color may be represented as hexadecimal RGB triples, as in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"HTML, or as hexadecimal ARGB tuples, with the A indicating alpha of transparency. An alpha value of 00 is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"totally transparent; FF is totally opaque. If RGB is used, the A value is assumed to be FF."}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLColor"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","role":"collection","title":"IvorMXL","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter."}]}}}